      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Papillary fibroelastoma is a rare, benign cardiac valve tumour, which can mimic conditions such as atrial myxoma and infective endocarditis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "CASE REPORT",
          "content": "An elderly lady presented with shortness of breath and chest pain and a mass on echocardiogram, which was confirmed on surgical excision to be a papillary fibroelastoma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "DISCUSSION",
          "content": "There were aspects of this lady's case that caused confusion over the diagnosis and showed how rare conditions can cause diagnostic problems."
        }
      ]},
